# Green Freedom Academy

## Mission

Green Freedom Academy helps teachers create high-quality P.6 English lessons, worksheets, games, and assessments quickly. **The goal is to save teachers time** — not to add complexity.

## Product Principles

1. Teacher-first design
2. Technology makes teachers' work easier
3. Thai is the default UI language
4. Primary focus: P.6 English
5. Student loop: **Learn → Short Practice → Game**
6. Preserve existing working functionality
7. Reusable components and maintainable TypeScript
8. Support desktop, tablet, and mobile
9. Explain major refactoring before implementing
10. Every code change must pass `npm run build` before completion

## North-Star Flow (PLANNED / FUTURE)

AI Teaching Brain → Lesson Generator → Classroom Companion → Worksheet Generator → Game Generator → Assessment Generator → Teacher Studio / Student Experience

Most stages are **not implemented** — see `docs/02-ROADMAP.md`.

## Tech Stack

Next.js 15 · React 19 · TypeScript · Supabase (schema defined; **not connected in app**)

## Current State (Do Not Assume)

- Demo UI works: `/`, `/login`, `/student`, `/teacher`, `/lesson/present-simple`
- Auth is demo-only (`localStorage`); Supabase client in `lib/supabase-browser.ts` is **unused**
- Practice, Game, AI generators, worksheets, and assessments are **not built**

## Coding Rules

- Never delete working features unless requested
- Functional React components; avoid `any`
- Use `@/` imports; extend `app/globals.css` tokens — no new CSS framework without approval
- Thai for UI copy; English for code identifiers and grammar examples
- Minimal diffs; extract components when patterns repeat
- Update `docs/10-CHANGELOG.md` and roadmap when shipping features

